{# Public-page shell composition.

   header_html: pre-rendered nav snippet | ''
   footer_html: pre-rendered footer snippet | ''
   body_html:   inner page body (h1 + blocks)
   max_width_px: '576px' | '672px' | ... | '100%' — body wrapper cap

   Header / footer sit OUTSIDE the per-page max-width body wrapper so
   their own .sp-nav-inner / .sp-footer-inner cap (max-w-5xl) drives
   chrome width independently from the body's max_width — keeps the
   nav identical across "/", any /page/view~slug, and pages with
   different max_width settings. #}
{{ header_html | raw }}
{# w-full: this div is a flex item all the way up to <body> (flex flex-col),
   and a `width:auto` flex item's cross-axis stretch still bottoms out at its
   own content's min-content size — min-w-0 alone does NOT override that for
   stretch sizing (only for flex-shrink on the main axis). A wide child (e.g.
   the cookies-table's `white-space: nowrap` mobile rule, .md-preview table)
   then grew this div past the viewport instead of scrolling inside the
   table itself. An explicit width gives the div a definite size, which
   sidesteps the automatic-minimum-size stretch clamp entirely. #}
<div style="max-width:{{ max_width_px }}" class="mx-auto px-4 py-8 w-full">
    {{ body_html | raw }}
</div>
{{ footer_html | raw }}
